#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1402
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editor Component Extensions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"editor-component-plugins\">Editor Component Extensions</"
"link> extend KatePart, the Advanced Text Editor component used within many "
"&kde; applications, such as &kate;, &kwrite;, Kile, and KDevelop. Creating "
"an Editor Component Plugin will allow you to extend the editor's "
"functionality in any and all of these programs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To get started, see the <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Development/"
"Tutorials/Kate/KTextEditor_Plugins\"> KTextEditor Plugin Tutorial on &kde; "
"TechBase</ulink>. For even more, see the <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde."
"org/Development/Tutorials/Kate/KTextEditor_Plugins_Advanced\"> Advanced "
"Tutorial, also on TechBase</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find the <ulink url=\"http://api.kde.org/4.10-api/kdelibs-apidocs/"
"interfaces/ktexteditor/html/\"> complete API documentation in the &kde; API "
"Reference</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1423
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; (C++) Application Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"kate-application-plugins\">Kate Application Plugins</link> "
"extend the functionality of the &kate; editor itself in any way you can "
"imagine, using the same programming language &kate; is written in, C++."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To get started, see the <ulink url=\"http://kate-editor.org/2004/01/06/"
"writing-a-kate-plugin/\">Writing a &kate; Plugin tutorial on the &kate; "
"website</ulink>. There is also <ulink url=\"http://quickgit.kde.org/?p=kate."
"git&amp;a=tree&amp;f=addons%2Fkate%2Fhelloworld\"> a classic <quote>Hello, "
"world!</quote> example plugin included with the &kate; source code</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1439
#, no-c-format
msgid "&pate; Python Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"pate\">&pate; Plugins</link> also allow you to extend the "
"functionality of &kate; in any way you like, using the Python programming "
"language."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To get started, see the <ulink url=\"http://kate-editor.org/2012/07/01/"
"python-plugin-developer-guide-part-1/\"> Python plugin developer guide on "
"the &kate; website</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also access the API reference in the <link linkend=\"pate-config"
"\">&pate; Configuration</link> screen."
msgstr ""

